{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357039-what-nova-age-tech-is-still-used-on-22nd-century-earth","id":1357039,"title":"What Nova Age Tech is still used on 22nd Century Earth","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-26T06:30:58-08:00","id":1357039,"title":"What Nova Age Tech is still used on 22nd Century Earth","content":"The big ones I am aware of are Hyperfusion and Gravity Crystals. I suppose technically the OpNet is a Nova Invention? Is there still eufiber in use anywhere, knowingly or possibly not? Clearly any notice biotech is not Nova Derived but even some mundane hard tech possibly has roots in the nova age, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T06:53:15-08:00","id":1357042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tragedyjones</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357039-what-nova-age-tech-is-still-used-on-22nd-century-earth#post1357039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big ones I am aware of are Hyperfusion and Gravity Crystals. I suppose technically the OpNet is a Nova Invention? Is there still eufiber in use anywhere, knowingly or possibly not? Clearly any notice biotech is not Nova Derived but even some mundane hard tech possibly has roots in the nova age, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Figure that unless a different hardtech replacement was better, eufiber would be in use in places like the FSA or Nihonjin. Basically anywhere that Psions and Biotech would be regarded with suspicion and hostility. Figure in most other places eufiber got torn out and replaced due to concerns about Aberrant manipulations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T09:24:33-08:00","id":1357055,"title":"","content":"While Buendia was indeed a nova, the eufiber they invented is a synthetic carbon polymer. It's baseline tech and the principles behind it are widely understood. It continues to power the OpNet well into the 22nd century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T09:35:04-08:00","id":1357058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357039-what-nova-age-tech-is-still-used-on-22nd-century-earth?p=1357055#post1357055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Buendia was indeed a nova, the eufiber they invented is a synthetic carbon polymer. It's baseline tech and the principles behind it are widely understood. It continues to power the OpNet well into the 22nd century.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you be so kind as to share what an example of &quot;illegal nova age tech&quot; would look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T09:53:57-08:00","id":1357063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tragedyjones</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357039-what-nova-age-tech-is-still-used-on-22nd-century-earth?p=1357058#post1357058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you be so kind as to share what an example of &quot;illegal nova age tech&quot; would look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>No books to hand right now, but that stuff that allowed for computer-based &quot;telepathy&quot; and also allowed some Novas to effectively hack/control people. Otherwise figure anything defined as &quot;Nova-tech&quot; (which requires Novas manufacture/repair/etc) or Q-Tech. The latter is a little irrelevant because the only ones likely to use it are actual Novas. Figure Nova-tech is either illegal because making it means making deals with Aberrants or just super-duper rare because Novas aren't around to make/fix it anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T11:42:33-08:00","id":1357076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tragedyjones</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357039-what-nova-age-tech-is-still-used-on-22nd-century-earth?p=1357058#post1357058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you be so kind as to share what an example of &quot;illegal nova age tech&quot; would look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Brain implants in the vein of Matrix or Johnny Mnemonic. Artificial Sentience. Unrestricted nanotech. <br /> <br /> Most Q-tech is irrelevant without a source of quantum, so without novas, they're effectively useless. Still, \u00c6on would like to keep their hands on it, just in case.<br /> <br /> A lot of it is hard to quantify. Trinity 1e had a story about early Qin diplomacy: they gave their human hosts a piece of biotech. Humans studied the intricacies of it for weeks before going back to the Qin and asking what it was? The Qin looked confused and said &quot;a vase.&quot;<br /> <br /> From the Qin, our allies, it's an amusing story of clashing cultures, and also serves to demonstrate their mastery of biotech over humans' capabilities. If that same item came from an Aberrant? Well, fuck. Put it in isolation. Sure, it <i>might</i> just be a vase, but who knows? It's a ticking time bomb. Maybe it'll explode. Maybe it'll infect everyone who touches it with some weird corruption virus. Maybe it'll remain inert for the first 1000 touches and <i>then</i> activate. There's no way to know. Aberrant powers don't obey the laws of physics. Best stick it in a deep dark hole and try to forget about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T04:53:41-08:00","id":1357742,"title":"","content":"The thing is, suppressing information about Q-tech, not just the items themselves, is the justification for the rebooted Project Rewrite. By definition it can't be duplicated by non-Novas. Either they're deluded about it's nature or they have a hidden agenda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2893-muon","name":"muon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T15:02:17-08:00","id":1357887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357039-what-nova-age-tech-is-still-used-on-22nd-century-earth?p=1357742#post1357742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, suppressing information about Q-tech, not just the items themselves, is the justification for the rebooted Project Rewrite. By definition it can't be duplicated by non-Novas. Either they're deluded about it's nature or they have a hidden agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div>We as the players/GMs of this game setting know that Q-Tech can't be duplicated by non-Novas (and there could easily be a supplement a couple-three years from now detailing how that could be done). The people living in the setting don't know that. Also, while they're rare, there are still Novas in the setting. And most them are coming to rape/kill/eat us all. So maybe publishing what could easily end up as a hot-to manual for Q-Tech that they can use to build stuff to help them rape/kill/eat us isn't a smart move.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T16:05:18-08:00","id":1357893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357039-what-nova-age-tech-is-still-used-on-22nd-century-earth?p=1357742#post1357742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, suppressing information about Q-tech, not just the items themselves, is the justification for the rebooted Project Rewrite. By definition it can't be duplicated by non-Novas. Either they're deluded about it's nature or they have a hidden agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div>It couldn\u2019t be duplicated by non-novas 200 years ago with then-existing tech. Technology has advanced, and while most q-tech still can\u2019t be copied directly, studying it with AEon-era tech understanding might allow parts to be understood or functions to be copied. Iron-Man suits and mechs were impossible 200 years before AEon, now VARGs aren\u2019t that hard to manufacture. Near AI was impossible now SIs are everywhere - and they\u2019re only SI and not AI because of international agreement.<br /> <br /> And the biggest danger of all was that as novas felt increasingly alienated from baselines (and competitive/paranoid about each other) they started building more elaborate booby-traps into their inventions. That thing you find might be inert for you, or it might boil the flesh from your bones if you try and activate it. Or it might set of a nuclear explosion. Or it might download a virtual duplicate into your brain and go on a rampage on behalf of the ex-nova.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T17:02:50-08:00","id":1357899,"title":"","content":"Not only that, but by the Aberrant war, it was very likely a lot of teh nova inventors were mega-int 5, possibly more (I don't know if there's still the intent to allow high quantum novas to break that cap a'la first edition or if it's a hard cap). Mega int five... is just beyond anything you can imagine. Even perfectly ordinary tech, stuff that doesn't incorporate nova power, could be dangerous and incomprehensible.<br /> <br /> My take on why it's banned comes from a Vernor Vinge novel--a fire upon the deep. It starts with an expedition finding a data vault of an ascended power. And they're very careful. They evaluate every step in the menu driven design process. But the problem is, compared to what created the archive, <i>they're smart apes</i>. And before long, without knowing it, the entire system is compromised, with their systems feeding them the data the creature wants them to see--until it's too late to do anything. <br /> <br /> That, I expect if the fear of a lot of advanced nova tech. And given the challenges of the world, you can bet the ban wsan't casually arrived at. Aeon and the nations of the earth probably got burned a <i>lot</i> before they finally decided: we can't risk it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}